// Title: Wmiprvse Wbemcomn DLL Hijack - File
// Sigma ID: 614a7e17-5643-4d89-b6fe-f9df1a79641c
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez (Cyb3rWard0g), OTR (Open Threat Research)
// Date: 2020-10-12 | Modified: 2022-12-02
// ATT&CK: execution, T1047, lateral-movement, T1021.002
// Description: Detects a threat actor creating a file named `wbemcomn.dll` in the `C:\Windows\System32\wbem\`
//   directory over the network and loading it for a WMI DLL Hijack scenario.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://threathunterplaybook.com/hunts/windows/201009-RemoteWMIWbemcomnDLLHijack/notebook.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_wmiprvse_wbemcomn_dll_hijack.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "System" and FolderPath endswith "\\wbem\\wbemcomn.dll"
